The '''Indian Institutes of Technology''' ('''IITs''') are a network of autonomous [[Central university (India)|public]] [[Institute of technology|engineering, technology and research universities]] in [[India]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/op-ed/too-many-iits-unrealistic-expectations/article33883323.ece|title=Too many IITs, unrealistic expectations|first=Philip G. Altbach & Eldho|last=Mathews|date=20 February 2021|via=www.thehindu.com}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.indiatoday.in/education-today/news/story/why-iit-bombay-iit-delhi-remain-top-picks-in-jee-advanced-2025-admissions-2778051-2025-08-28|title=Why IIT Bombay, IIT Delhi remain top picks in JEE Advanced 2025 admissions|first=India Today Education|last=Desk|date=28 August 2025|website=India Today}}</ref> Established in 1950, they are under the purview of the [[Ministry of Education (India)|Ministry of Education]] of the [[Government of India]] and are governed by the [[Institutes of Technology Act, 1961]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/iits-top-education-ministrys-rankings-for-2021/article36376187.ece|title=IITs top Education Ministry’s rankings for 2021|first=Special|last=Correspondent|date=9 September 2021|via=www.thehindu.com}}</ref>

The Act designates them as [[Institutes of National Importance]] and lays down their powers, duties, and governance framework as the country's premier institutions in the field of technology.<ref name="IITAct">{{cite web |url=https://www.iitsystem.ac.in/|title=Institutes of Technology Act, 1961 |website=IIT System Portal |access-date=17 September 2025}}</ref> There are currently 23 IITs functioning under this act.<ref name="HindustanTimes">{{cite web|url=http://www.hindustantimes.com/higherstudies/as-number-of-iits-increase-their-brand-value-diminishes/article1-1363608.aspx|title=Problem of plenty: As IITs multiply, the brand value diminishes|work=Hindustan Times|date=29 June 2015|access-date=17 September 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150831075125/http://www.hindustantimes.com/higherstudies/as-number-of-iits-increase-their-brand-value-diminishes/article1-1363608.aspx|archive-date=31 August 2015}}</ref> 
Each IIT operates autonomously and is linked to the others through a common council called the IIT Council, which oversees their administration. The [[Minister of Education (India)|Minister of Education]] serves as the [[ex officio]] chairperson of the IIT Council.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.iitsystem.ac.in/|title=IIT Council Portal|access-date=17 September 2025|archive-date=18 June 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190618184358/https://www.iitsystem.ac.in/}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/op-ed/the-iits-are-overcommitted-in-crisis/article67494448.ece|title=The IITs are overcommitted, in crisis|first=Philip G.|last=Altbach|date=4 November 2023|via=www.thehindu.com}}</ref>
